[test-suite name=hash ring=1
  [doc [#
conformance fixtures for cx-stdlib/hash (spec/std-lib/hash.md §6).

   Each program imports the bundled module via [?lib 'cx-stdlib/hash']
   (resolver MUST be quoted) then calls [$hash:fn args]. The LAST
   expression is the rendered result. Digests are bytes; fixtures render
   them through hash/format-hex (or *-hex convenience fns) so the
   out_text is a stable lowercase-hex string. Error fixtures use
   --- out_err with the bare CXER code.

   No inter-fixture [; comment ] dividers and no inline comments inside
   in_code: the fixture harness splits on `=== test:` then extracts each
   section to end-of-chunk, so any trailing comment after out_text would
   be swallowed into the expected value. Section grouping is by id range:
     001-006  empty + official non-empty digest vectors
     007-009  bytes/format-hex + string-convenience equivalence
     010-013  streaming == single-shot + purity
     014-017  BLAKE3 XOF prefix-extending property
     018-024  format conversion + round-trip + case
     025-028  constant-time equals
     029-032  SRI helpers + round-trip
     033-040  error codes (spec §5)

   Test vectors: SHA-256("")=e3b0c442...b7852b855, SHA-256("abc")=ba7816bf...f20015ad,
   SHA-384("")=38b060a7...4898b95b, SHA-512("")=cf83e135...927da3e,
   BLAKE3("")=af1349b9...e41f3262, BLAKE3("abc")=6437b3ac...d5bd9d85.
#]]

 [case id=hash-001-sha256-empty level=core
  [tags hash sha256-hex empty nist]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/hash']
[$hash:sha256-hex ""]
#]]
  [out-text [#
'e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855'
#]]
 ]

 [case id=hash-002-sha384-empty level=core
  [tags hash sha384-hex empty nist]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/hash']
[$hash:sha384-hex ""]
#]]
  [out-text [#
'38b060a751ac96384cd9327eb1b1e36a21fdb71114be07434c0cc7bf63f6e1da274edebfe76f65fbd51ad2f14898b95b'
#]]
 ]

